[1.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m━━━ Step 2 — the GitHub issue ━━━\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.004, "o", "\u001b[2m# A real issue lives at https://github.com/olafkfreund/aifactory-demo/issues/6\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.603, "o", "\u001b[2m# Title: 'Document the Quick Start in README'\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.603, "o", "\u001b[2m#   — the demo's existing spec walks through this end-to-end.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.609, "o", "\r\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\r\n  │ Document the Quick Start in README                       #6 │\r\n  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\r\n  │ Add a Quick Start section showing the three commands a new  │\r\n  │ user runs to bring the app up locally:                      │\r\n  │   pip install -e .                                          │\r\n  │   uvicorn src.app.main:app --reload                         │\r\n  │   curl http://localhost:8000/                               │\r\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\r\n\r\n"]
[2.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m━━━ Step 3 — /handover in Claude Code ━━━\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.006, "o", "\u001b[1mIn a Claude Code session in this repo, the developer types:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36m/handover\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe skill at \u001b[1m.claude/skills/handover/SKILL.md\u001b[0m reads the recent\r\nconversation, calls \u001b[1mmcp__aifactory__task_create_and_run\u001b[0m, and\r\nreturns a portal URL.  AIFactory's autonomous pipeline takes it\r\nfrom there.\r\n\r\n"]
[3.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m━━━ Step 4 — the spec AIFactory wrote ━━━\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.004, "o", "\u001b[2m# spec.md — what the planner agent crystallised from the issue body\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.603, "o", "\u001b[35m$\u001b[0m \u001b[1mcat /tmp/aifactory-demo/.aifactory/specs/019-gh23-document-the-quick-start-in-readme/spec.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.405, "o", "# Document the Quick Start in README\r\n\r\n**Source:** GitHub Issue [#23](https://github.com/olafkfreund/aifactory-demo/issues/23)\r\n**Labels:** documentation\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nAdd a **Quick Start** section to `README.md` in the `olafkfreund/aifactory-demo` repository. The section will show new users exactly three commands needed to clone, set up, and run the demo app locally. This addresses GitHub Issue #23 and improves the onboarding experience for first-time contributors and users.\r\n\r\n## Workflow Type\r\n\r\n`docs`\r\n\r\nThis is a documentation-only change. No application code, tests, or configuration files are modified. The sole deliverable is an updated `README.md` with a new Quick Start section.\r\n\r\n## Task Scope\r\n\r\n**In scope:**\r\n- Read existing `README.md` to determine correct insertion point for the new section\r\n- Inspect repo root files (`package.json`, `Makefile`, `flake.nix`, `docker-compose.yml`, etc.) to identify the canonical three setup commands\r\n- Add a `## Quick Start` section to `README.md` with exactly three commands in a fenced code block\r\n- Follow existing README formatting and style conventions\r\n- Reference (close) GitHub Issue #23 in the commit/PR message\r\n\r\n**Out of scope:**\r\n- Changes to application source code\r\n- Changes to CI/CD, tests, or configuration files\r\n- Adding more than three commands to the Quick Start section\r\n- Rewriting or restructuring existing README sections\r\n\r\n## Success Criteria\r\n\r\n- [ ] `README.md` contains a `## Quick Start` section\r\n- [ ] The Quick Start section documents exactly three commands (e.g., clone → install → run)\r\n- [ ] Commands are wrapped in a fenced code block with the correct language tag (e.g., `bash`)\r\n- [ ] Section is placed logically near the top of `README.md` (before detailed documentation)\r\n- [ ] Existing README content is preserved unchanged\r\n- [ ] The three commands are accurate and verified against actual repo setup files\r\n- [ ] PR/commit message references `Closes #23`\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nAdd a Quick Start section to README.md showing the three commands a new user runs to get the demo app running locally.\r\n"]
